  "final_answer": "I have all the information needed to provide a complete answer. The top beginner IoT course with a high rating has been identified.\n\n## Task Completed Successfully\n\nI found a beginner-level Coursera course on Internet of Things (IoT) with a high rating. Here are the details:\n\n### Course Information\n\n| Field | Details |\n|-------|---------|\n| **Course Name** | Introduction to Programming the Internet of Things (IoT) (物联网 (IoT) 编程入门) |\n| **Instructor** | **Ian Harris** (from University of California, Irvine) |\n| **Rating** | ⭐ **4.7 / 5** stars (based on 20,511 reviews) |\n| **Level** | **Beginner** (初级) — no prior experience required |\n| **Format** | Specialization (6-course series) |\n| **Duration** | ~2 months at 10 hours/week |\n| **Enrollment** | 187,966 students |\n| **Next Start Date** | September 25 |\n\n### Course Description\nDesign and create a simple IoT device in just six courses. The specialization covers embedded systems, the Raspberry Pi platform, and the Arduino environment for building devices that can control the physical world.\n\n### Skills You Will Gain (您将获得的技能)\n- **Linux commands** — Working with Linux operating system\n- **Embedded Systems** — Designing and programming embedded systems\n- **Electronics** — Working with electronic components and hardware\n- **Debugging** — Troubleshooting hardware and software issues\n- **Network Protocols** — Including TCP/IP and the OSI model\n- **Functional Specifications & Requirements** — Writing user requirements documents and functional specifications\n- **Basic Electrical Systems** — Foundational electrical engineering concepts\n- **Test Plans** — Creating and executing test plans\n- **Internet of Things (IoT)** — Core IoT principles and applications\n- **Python Programming** — Programming IoT devices\n\n### Tools You Will Learn\n- OSI Model, Operating Systems, Linux, Embedded Software, API, Python Programming\n\nThis course was selected because it matched all three criteria: (1) **Beginner level** — no prior experience required, (2) **High rating** — 4.7/5 from over 20,000 reviews, and (3) **IoT-focused** — explicitly about Internet of Things. It was the top result after applying the \"Beginner\" filter on the IoT search results page.",
